# delivery-relay-rln — two RLN-gated host peers that MEET AT A THIRD NODE and
# never dial each other. The relay is a container (harness/lib/relay.sh,
# image from tools/build-e2e-image.sh), so the hop is a real one.
#
# delivery-rln proves the RLN seam with the peers wired directly; this proves
# the topology delivery actually ships in, where a bootstrap node forwards.
# With E2E_RELAY_RLN=1 that relay also holds a membership and validates what
# it forwards.
NODES=2
NEEDS_MODULES="liblogos_lez_rln_module liblogos_rln_module delivery_module"
TARGETS="local"
# The relay image is a separate prerequisite — tools/build-e2e-image.sh.
# No PREFLIGHT_ANY: the flake pin (delivery-module v0.3.0-rc.2) carries the
# preset-resolved RLN this scenario needs, so nothing has to come from a
# checkout. DELIVERY_MODULE_CHECKOUT / LOGOS_DELIVERY_CHECKOUT still override
# it when you are testing an unreleased delivery tree.
RUNNER=bash
